{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1338547-break-out-the-crystals","id":1338547,"title":"Break out the crystals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-29T18:30:46-07:00","id":1338547,"title":"Break out the crystals","content":"A player of mine obsessed with psychics brought up the idea of Using various types of crystals for their supposed mystical properties...I was intrigued at the idea<br /> <br /> But how to implement? Passive bonuses, a merit, a whole subset of sorcery? <br /> <br /> Any advice or ideas from the community would be greatly appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T18:50:45-07:00","id":1338550,"title":"","content":"Could use them as a requirement for or way to get supernatural abilities, like to access the Medium ability, maybe with different crystals offering different modifiers or Resonances. Among supernatural it could tie into fetishes, rites, blood sorceries or yantras (they can be used among the acanthus), how Prometheans are made.<br /> <br /> The foreseeable issue is that micromanagement of gear isn't really a big Chronicles thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-29-2019, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T21:39:33-07:00","id":1338565,"title":"","content":"They make good focuses for Supernatural Merits, many of which need a particular focus, activity or instrument to invoke. That character's focus is needing access to particular kinds of crystals placed in particular arrangements. Particular types of crystal might also make good choices for the banes of ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> Unless you narrow down what the crystals are used to actually do, I wouldn't create a Using Crystals Merit or a subsystem of crystal sorcery or anything. When designing a new power, you want an idea of what it does and, just as importantly, an idea of what it <i>doesn't</i> do, and crystals are up there on the list of occult implements associated with Doing Basically Anything. They thus fare better as the paint that adds color to a base design.<br /> <br /> You could certainly make new Supernatural Merits for particular uses of crystals, likely broader practices for which the character, again, uses crystals as their focus. I could easily see a Supernatural Merit which makes a character especially good at abjuring and exorcising ghosts or spirits, for which crystals would again make a valid focus.<br /> <br /> I would definitely discourage trying to keep track of individual crystals and types of crystal. You could use the equipment rules to model &quot;collection of esoteric crystals&quot; as a piece of equipment, but the challenge in play likely isn't obtaining a particular stone, but in having access to your collected stones and the time and focus available to arrange them just right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}